[{:db/id 17592186119778 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7f0a84be-936b-55f9-b169-54a768974c12" "question-b1079762-fa86-56ef-a06d-de94245b17fa" "question-38d108f6-377b-5951-bc6b-4ec43d8b652b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119592 :question/problem "Given that ![](images/fc/fcc4c2fb5ffaf79bd40a967fa0f3ff3ed3c25a4bc91e831f679aa2162d93050b.svg) find ![](images/3a/3a950a6005df11dc3df83b40a796c8e5ce962b591e040207bb961da532ec92dd.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Given two ![](images/b0/b0cdde792f80dc6b0c5defb2f8d767ae115ecf922fa46f2a233f10959e509870.svg) matrices ![](images/34/34058a2a5d1de088feed7d9825ba218394c9a8bb880b046be7b47307cdd37ce1.svg) and ![](images/50/504b9ae6bd4255a78e26a2d32aaca2d613171ad01c9ac5d992f5512d093605e7.svg) we have\n\n![](images/3f/3fbf04c7a536c85422f2762eb5475ff5edfcff7a71eee0fa3cc14143e79bb10f.svg)\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n![](images/16/16c31a7e010da9d8f4e17628bc1c7b5dd3ef1d65a4e5e191bec2fd404135a7bc.svg)\n\nWe can compute the required determinants as follows:\n\n- For the first determinant, we notice that it's upper triangular. Therefore, the determinant is simply the product of the diagonal entries.\n\n- For the second determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion down the ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg)st column.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n![](images/27/273e8879a6f78121b98902852e974aef15d9408e7cd026d3cc17e51837248ede.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119779 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9e9ddda3-97aa-551d-9453-cae76713ec59" "question-37f105cd-9dd0-500b-bb29-7f9f80a1a14c" "question-0b58d794-d6a1-55fe-88d5-660b59bdd30a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119593 :question/problem "Find $|A^{-1}|,$ if  ![](images/8e/8e92cd7ddbecf627452e4fa63d2af25fc60fad228bf42b5c4f8c9dfad28f4971.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119780 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8c3dc4f1-ad56-595b-a7eb-41a85271c7fe" "question-80589b9c-bfb0-57bc-8e70-de307d877343"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119594 :question/problem "Given that \n![](images/58/589324d1b345360020e9c2b1096b64a08008a52b05a13fdc7fd39bcb063a8d58.svg)\nfind \n![](images/f4/f4925a93ca952863cac520a853c1bc5d7c815dc8324043d6c0963d20d2b2b1ff.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-7f0a84be-936b-55f9-b169-54a768974c12" :question/id #uuid "7f0a84be-936b-55f9-b169-54a768974c12" :question/math-academy-id "q-42577" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(A)=det[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe can compute the required determinants as follows:\n\n- For the first determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row.\n\n- For the second determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion down the $2$nd column.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\cdot 1(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2-1)\\cdot (8-6) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-db7de380-466f-5089-9f2e-e91927307109"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-db7de380-466f-5089-9f2e-e91927307109" :answer-field/id #uuid "db7de380-466f-5089-9f2e-e91927307109" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1de3d101-6ebd-5bbc-ad0b-5f1d9ed17bbf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2f0dcd3-6430-515f-8e85-02e0bf1c5fa4" "answer-3896dbb3-7bb1-5f7c-b8bf-88d4cf58a131" "answer-1de3d101-6ebd-5bbc-ad0b-5f1d9ed17bbf" "answer-e50a27dc-031b-52dd-8815-f79824db9e9c" "answer-dd787881-42cf-53fe-9c3e-08b97bcc5ccf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2f0dcd3-6430-515f-8e85-02e0bf1c5fa4" :answer/id #uuid "d2f0dcd3-6430-515f-8e85-02e0bf1c5fa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3896dbb3-7bb1-5f7c-b8bf-88d4cf58a131" :answer/id #uuid "3896dbb3-7bb1-5f7c-b8bf-88d4cf58a131" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1de3d101-6ebd-5bbc-ad0b-5f1d9ed17bbf" :answer/id #uuid "1de3d101-6ebd-5bbc-ad0b-5f1d9ed17bbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e50a27dc-031b-52dd-8815-f79824db9e9c" :answer/id #uuid "e50a27dc-031b-52dd-8815-f79824db9e9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd787881-42cf-53fe-9c3e-08b97bcc5ccf" :answer/id #uuid "dd787881-42cf-53fe-9c3e-08b97bcc5ccf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120449 :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(A)=det[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(5\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2)\\cdot (3\\cdot 2\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =(-10)\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =120.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118808 :answer-field/correct 17592186118809 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-b1079762-fa86-56ef-a06d-de94245b17fa" :question/id #uuid "b1079762-fa86-56ef-a06d-de94245b17fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-130474" :question/problem "Given that $C=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(C).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(C)=det[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe can compute the required determinants as follows:\n\n- For the first determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row.\n\n- For the second determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion down the $2$nd column.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\cdot (-1)(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(6-4)\\cdot (-1)(12-5) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-57142131-309b-5e63-93f0-085dd8ef09bd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-57142131-309b-5e63-93f0-085dd8ef09bd" :answer-field/id #uuid "57142131-309b-5e63-93f0-085dd8ef09bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7dd0e1b8-d837-556e-96c2-a100f45e8fe7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b4fdf14b-3a08-5a96-9420-377d1a8d1538" "answer-7dd0e1b8-d837-556e-96c2-a100f45e8fe7" "answer-daea1037-0203-5328-a357-a7d37817bb29" "answer-0a0c86ff-0d80-5008-95a2-bec3a1c1a808" "answer-11030227-d4ce-5b70-8894-186891176d6b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4fdf14b-3a08-5a96-9420-377d1a8d1538" :answer/id #uuid "b4fdf14b-3a08-5a96-9420-377d1a8d1538" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dd0e1b8-d837-556e-96c2-a100f45e8fe7" :answer/id #uuid "7dd0e1b8-d837-556e-96c2-a100f45e8fe7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-daea1037-0203-5328-a357-a7d37817bb29" :answer/id #uuid "daea1037-0203-5328-a357-a7d37817bb29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a0c86ff-0d80-5008-95a2-bec3a1c1a808" :answer/id #uuid "0a0c86ff-0d80-5008-95a2-bec3a1c1a808" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11030227-d4ce-5b70-8894-186891176d6b" :answer/id #uuid "11030227-d4ce-5b70-8894-186891176d6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-38d108f6-377b-5951-bc6b-4ec43d8b652b" :question/id #uuid "38d108f6-377b-5951-bc6b-4ec43d8b652b" :question/math-academy-id "q-88281" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(A)=det[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2)\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot 3\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-633fd2f4-984e-51bc-b51a-5f37a89e06b4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-633fd2f4-984e-51bc-b51a-5f37a89e06b4" :answer-field/id #uuid "633fd2f4-984e-51bc-b51a-5f37a89e06b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-755ff62c-e4b0-56e4-8933-fdd296936d8f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b74bd5d3-d00b-534f-908c-090b06c3201d" "answer-9577d942-a37d-5bb6-ad63-4cff94938a48" "answer-755ff62c-e4b0-56e4-8933-fdd296936d8f" "answer-c498389f-d133-538a-bef9-88e693ebc92c" "answer-44a67a7f-7ce3-5fc4-9a99-c7b43778cf51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b74bd5d3-d00b-534f-908c-090b06c3201d" :answer/id #uuid "b74bd5d3-d00b-534f-908c-090b06c3201d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9577d942-a37d-5bb6-ad63-4cff94938a48" :answer/id #uuid "9577d942-a37d-5bb6-ad63-4cff94938a48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-755ff62c-e4b0-56e4-8933-fdd296936d8f" :answer/id #uuid "755ff62c-e4b0-56e4-8933-fdd296936d8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c498389f-d133-538a-bef9-88e693ebc92c" :answer/id #uuid "c498389f-d133-538a-bef9-88e693ebc92c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "76" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44a67a7f-7ce3-5fc4-9a99-c7b43778cf51" :answer/id #uuid "44a67a7f-7ce3-5fc4-9a99-c7b43778cf51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "77" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9e9ddda3-97aa-551d-9453-cae76713ec59" :question/id #uuid "9e9ddda3-97aa-551d-9453-cae76713ec59" :question/math-academy-id "q-43070" :question/problem "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =10-5 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a81cf8c4-10bc-54bc-9308-65fe3b30e2ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a81cf8c4-10bc-54bc-9308-65fe3b30e2ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "a81cf8c4-10bc-54bc-9308-65fe3b30e2ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd130b49-aec7-5947-9ffc-20dcb30a8a97" :answer-field/choices ["answer-341db512-89dd-5d60-9521-449fcc83f4d2" "answer-1657176b-b7bb-5bac-8681-50357708185d" "answer-15bb6772-ebfa-5300-9707-f0c44ba3ca38" "answer-bd130b49-aec7-5947-9ffc-20dcb30a8a97" "answer-7ecdfc0d-790a-509f-8041-8c18f54a719a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-341db512-89dd-5d60-9521-449fcc83f4d2" :answer/id #uuid "341db512-89dd-5d60-9521-449fcc83f4d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1657176b-b7bb-5bac-8681-50357708185d" :answer/id #uuid "1657176b-b7bb-5bac-8681-50357708185d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15bb6772-ebfa-5300-9707-f0c44ba3ca38" :answer/id #uuid "15bb6772-ebfa-5300-9707-f0c44ba3ca38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd130b49-aec7-5947-9ffc-20dcb30a8a97" :answer/id #uuid "bd130b49-aec7-5947-9ffc-20dcb30a8a97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ecdfc0d-790a-509f-8041-8c18f54a719a" :answer/id #uuid "7ecdfc0d-790a-509f-8041-8c18f54a719a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-37f105cd-9dd0-500b-bb29-7f9f80a1a14c" :question/id #uuid "37f105cd-9dd0-500b-bb29-7f9f80a1a14c" :question/math-academy-id "q-43071" :question/problem "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6-2 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-660640e3-e8ef-509a-a758-3c65a1428537"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-660640e3-e8ef-509a-a758-3c65a1428537" :answer-field/id #uuid "660640e3-e8ef-509a-a758-3c65a1428537" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-90c1ce8c-7b18-5377-9a47-ace432f229bc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3dafe486-15fc-5abc-8a0d-2beb22386f42" "answer-cc7cb828-c853-54d8-b205-d802c97b37f2" "answer-8e814c6a-3786-561d-9f46-38ef12a0585a" "answer-90c1ce8c-7b18-5377-9a47-ace432f229bc" "answer-d2b62576-113c-5f4d-b29d-3ce30a3f8585"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3dafe486-15fc-5abc-8a0d-2beb22386f42" :answer/id #uuid "3dafe486-15fc-5abc-8a0d-2beb22386f42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc7cb828-c853-54d8-b205-d802c97b37f2" :answer/id #uuid "cc7cb828-c853-54d8-b205-d802c97b37f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e814c6a-3786-561d-9f46-38ef12a0585a" :answer/id #uuid "8e814c6a-3786-561d-9f46-38ef12a0585a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90c1ce8c-7b18-5377-9a47-ace432f229bc" :answer/id #uuid "90c1ce8c-7b18-5377-9a47-ace432f229bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2b62576-113c-5f4d-b29d-3ce30a3f8585" :answer/id #uuid "d2b62576-113c-5f4d-b29d-3ce30a3f8585" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0b58d794-d6a1-55fe-88d5-660b59bdd30a" :question/id #uuid "0b58d794-d6a1-55fe-88d5-660b59bdd30a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42578" :question/problem "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =20-18 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-75968549-80b9-5200-918a-66a961c78ce2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-75968549-80b9-5200-918a-66a961c78ce2" :answer-field/id #uuid "75968549-80b9-5200-918a-66a961c78ce2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bb525c0d-2a19-503f-b30d-3b12439ddf16" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b75e75d9-4872-5fbc-a59d-3e54eebab508" "answer-cab0cf74-f931-5eb5-9974-e3db30298fa7" "answer-5725181a-ff3e-5107-8722-cd79c0a511e2" "answer-bb525c0d-2a19-503f-b30d-3b12439ddf16" "answer-336cb96e-8d35-5f9f-92e4-bf01f1fe608d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b75e75d9-4872-5fbc-a59d-3e54eebab508" :answer/id #uuid "b75e75d9-4872-5fbc-a59d-3e54eebab508" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cab0cf74-f931-5eb5-9974-e3db30298fa7" :answer/id #uuid "cab0cf74-f931-5eb5-9974-e3db30298fa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5725181a-ff3e-5107-8722-cd79c0a511e2" :answer/id #uuid "5725181a-ff3e-5107-8722-cd79c0a511e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb525c0d-2a19-503f-b30d-3b12439ddf16" :answer/id #uuid "bb525c0d-2a19-503f-b30d-3b12439ddf16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-336cb96e-8d35-5f9f-92e4-bf01f1fe608d" :answer/id #uuid "336cb96e-8d35-5f9f-92e4-bf01f1fe608d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8c3dc4f1-ad56-595b-a7eb-41a85271c7fe" :question/id #uuid "8c3dc4f1-ad56-595b-a7eb-41a85271c7fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-130693" :question/problem "Find\n$|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 114 & 210 & 198 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $2$nd row of our determinant is almost equal to the $3$rd row. So, we can rewrite the given determinant, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 114 & 210 & 198 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 113+1 & 210+0 & 198+0 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 113+1 & 210+0 & 198+0 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first determinant must be zero since it has two identical rows, while the second determinant can be expanded across the $2$nd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 113 & 210 & 198\\end{aligned}| & =0+1(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 210 & 198\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4\\cdot 198-2\\cdot 210) \\\\  & =-(792-420) \\\\  & =-372\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-96ea088a-9b87-51d6-9259-b1c59aec445a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-96ea088a-9b87-51d6-9259-b1c59aec445a" :answer-field/id #uuid "96ea088a-9b87-51d6-9259-b1c59aec445a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dd980cfa-ae7f-54ba-bba4-12f039277176" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2f66b246-867d-5382-b745-224f4b0b1960" "answer-e9605807-1150-5819-807b-86c3f17e6ec2" "answer-dd980cfa-ae7f-54ba-bba4-12f039277176" "answer-bbaccfd8-0fee-5b02-b497-78e555afcf98" "answer-6f34b981-25b3-5127-9dcc-d184355dec85"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f66b246-867d-5382-b745-224f4b0b1960" :answer/id #uuid "2f66b246-867d-5382-b745-224f4b0b1960" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-276" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9605807-1150-5819-807b-86c3f17e6ec2" :answer/id #uuid "e9605807-1150-5819-807b-86c3f17e6ec2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-346" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd980cfa-ae7f-54ba-bba4-12f039277176" :answer/id #uuid "dd980cfa-ae7f-54ba-bba4-12f039277176" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-372" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bbaccfd8-0fee-5b02-b497-78e555afcf98" :answer/id #uuid "bbaccfd8-0fee-5b02-b497-78e555afcf98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "294" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f34b981-25b3-5127-9dcc-d184355dec85" :answer/id #uuid "6f34b981-25b3-5127-9dcc-d184355dec85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "429" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-80589b9c-bfb0-57bc-8e70-de307d877343" :question/id #uuid "80589b9c-bfb0-57bc-8e70-de307d877343" :question/math-academy-id "q-88306" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300 & 270 & 100 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $1$st row of our determinant is almost equal to the $2$nd row. So, we can rewrite the given determinant, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300 & 270 & 100 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300+0 & 250+20 & 100+0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300+0 & 250+20 & 100+0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 0 & 20 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first determinant must be zero since it has two identical rows, while the second determinant can be expanded across the $2$nd row, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}300 & 250 & 100 \\\\ 0 & 20 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0+20(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}300 & 100 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =20\\cdot (300\\cdot 1-100\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =20\\cdot 200 \\\\  & =4\\,000\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-db1d1fba-e4ba-50df-bd35-d24e24ca86ab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-db1d1fba-e4ba-50df-bd35-d24e24ca86ab" :answer-field/id #uuid "db1d1fba-e4ba-50df-bd35-d24e24ca86ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-256655f5-3716-5c72-b038-769fa376cf93" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e3f48478-6c84-5d48-9002-c26925eb220f" "answer-65294e4c-a8db-5c12-befc-326f1199fa33" "answer-6c92f4c3-474c-5da4-bd3e-a7ddf9353c60" "answer-b440a564-08a1-5c84-a502-ec561384a59f" "answer-256655f5-3716-5c72-b038-769fa376cf93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3f48478-6c84-5d48-9002-c26925eb220f" :answer/id #uuid "e3f48478-6c84-5d48-9002-c26925eb220f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65294e4c-a8db-5c12-befc-326f1199fa33" :answer/id #uuid "65294e4c-a8db-5c12-befc-326f1199fa33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c92f4c3-474c-5da4-bd3e-a7ddf9353c60" :answer/id #uuid "6c92f4c3-474c-5da4-bd3e-a7ddf9353c60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,700" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b440a564-08a1-5c84-a502-ec561384a59f" :answer/id #uuid "b440a564-08a1-5c84-a502-ec561384a59f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-256655f5-3716-5c72-b038-769fa376cf93" :answer/id #uuid "256655f5-3716-5c72-b038-769fa376cf93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121022 :tutorial/content "In this topic, we will consider a few more properties of determinants. Let's start with the following important property. \n\n*The determinant of the product of two square matrices is equal to the product of the determinants.*\n\nSymbolically, if ![](images/34/34058a2a5d1de088feed7d9825ba218394c9a8bb880b046be7b47307cdd37ce1.svg) and ![](images/25/256531b7f0ddb14dd11a59a3019a3361f1607d3fe16fa6d530a461344de8f39e.svg) are both square matrices, then\n\n![](images/e5/e59b47ca5462a066093945e2698404e595a92e9e70a2b8c4f8b2f30df9c9fbf1.svg)\n\nFor instance, suppose that we want to find the determinant of the matrix ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) that is defined as follows:\n![](images/9a/9a705ea4bd482cdf83251288108b48ff5bc7354c9d51c1b710b9e734c8a32dea.svg)\n\nTo easily compute ![](images/da/dab9a65c1cba3cd9f271a1910b060e5428813107b3b54945776aab3839003d45.svg), we first compute the determinants of the two matrices and then multiply the results. Also, notice that both matrices in our product are triangular, so their determinants are given by the product of the diagonal entries:\n\n![](images/fa/fa4214541c12b0a761fd7cb17f4efc2f6b4be2c1424094483a3c2f61ab63c0a0.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119996 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
